MOTD(5)                        P32W Unix                         MOTD(5)

NAME
       motd - message of the day

DESCRIPTION
       login(1) copies /etc/motd to the terminal after a successful
       login, before it starts the user's shell. Root may edit it
       to tell users of news, such as a coming shutdown. If the
       file is missing nothing is printed. The file as shipped
       holds

              Welcome to P32W Unix.

FILES
       /etc/motd

SEE ALSO
       login(1), rc(8)

BUGS
       There is no way for one user to turn it off (no
       .hushlogin), and su(1) does not print it.
